Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:44:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] input_form text: XLM-R tokenizer; one sentence per instance
 with value level

Two fixes to 0076 found in review on WZ, before any training:

- Tokenizer: the instruction encoder is XLM-R (vlnbert_init.py builds it
  from bert_config/xlm-roberta-base; instructions are padded with 1). 0076
  tokenised map sentences with BERT, whose ids index unrelated XLM-R word
  pieces. MapTextTokenizer now loads bert_config/xlm-roberta-base with
  AutoTokenizer (local files only; <s>=0, </s>=2, pad=1, checked).
- Content: one sentence per category merged every instance and dropped the
  cell value. Sentences are now one per 8-connected component (instance) of
  each nonzero channel on the downsampled grid, with its cell count, value
  level (legacy cache: 0.6 / 1.0), center and extent. The remaining loss
  versus the raster is the exact shape inside each instance's bounding box.

On the R2R_val_unseen_895 GT map: 30 sentences, at most 40 tokens each.
Raster path unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
